From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: a client the server cannot reach does not end the title.

get_handle_fd sends the descriptor with send_client_fd, which kills a client it cannot reach (EPIPE: the process is
ending, as a test's child at its exit), and the requesting thread with it, so current is NULL afterwards. Patch 2076's
lease then read current->process: the title's in-process server faulted at address 0x88 (req_get_handle_fd+0x12f,
called from main_loop) and the whole title ended, every other program with it (the milestone sweep on 2026-10-26,
during i386 ntdll file). The lease is now taken only while the thread is alive.
---
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index 20d5991..193e66c 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -3422,7 +3422,11 @@ DECL_HANDLER(get_handle_fd)
             reply->access = get_handle_access( current->process, req->handle );
             send_client_fd( current->process, unix_fd, req->handle );
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
-            if (reply->cacheable && ps5_is_child_process( current->process )) ps5_lease_take( current->process, req->handle );
+            /* send_client_fd kills a client it cannot reach (EPIPE: the process is ending), and current with it: the
+             * title's server then read current->process at NULL and the whole title ended (sweep 2026-10-26, i386
+             * ntdll file, req_get_handle_fd+0x12f, fault address 0x88) */
+            if (current && reply->cacheable && ps5_is_child_process( current->process ))
+                ps5_lease_take( current->process, req->handle );
 #endif
         }
         release_object( fd );
